<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,325.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,325.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,325 today from 1,320 on June 30, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1394    12.656	  1395    12.669</p>
<p>   1a   1325 10038.000	  1324 10025.000</p>
<p>   2    1593    22.763	  1579    22.563</p>
<p>   2a   1563 12819.000	  1564 12825.000</p>
<p>   3    1392    12.844	  1382    12.750</p>
